      "one line solution - Javascript | Easy brijesh178 11 225 Aug 28, 2023 JavaScript Complexity \n \n Time complexity: O(n) \n \n\n \n Space complexity: O(n) \n \n\n Code \n  \n var   isAcronym   =   function   ( words ,  s )   { \n    return  s  ===  words . map ( ( str )   =>  str [ 0 ] ) . join ( \"\" ) \n } Comments (2) Elia1984 Jan 06, 2024 Brilliant! 1 Reply Mohanraj_Murugasen Oct 16, 2023 Great @brijesh, Innovative idea. 1 Reply",
      "[JavaScript] One-line efficient solution ✔💯✅ ab_noori 42 150 Nov 17, 2023 JavaScript isAcronym   =   ( words ,  s )   =>  s  ===  words . map (   w   =>  w [ 0 ] ) . join ( '' ) \n \n Please upvote ⇑, if you find it efficient 🥰 Comments (2) kontadorlol Dec 18, 2023 nice 1 Show 1 Replies Reply sazishaliakbar Nov 17, 2023 efficient solution 0 Reply",
      "One-liner without creating any string - 71 ms eforce 292 419 Aug 19, 2023 JavaScript Complexity \n \n \n Time complexity: \n O(n)O(n) O ( n ) \n \n \n Space complexity: \n O(1)O(1) O ( 1 ) \n \n \n Code \n  \n var   isAcronym   =   function ( words ,  s )   { \n      return  words . length   ===  s . length   &&  words . every ( ( v ,  i )   =>  v [ 0 ]   ===  s [ i ] ) ; \n } ; Comments (2) vivekjain202 Aug 20, 2023 Read more 1 Show 2 Replies Reply KondalDurgam Feb 01, 2024 Great solution broo, 0 Reply",
      "All Solutions Simple and Efficient Solution | Fully Explained 💯 | Javascript 🔥💯 RockAdil 24 229 Aug 19, 2023 JavaScript Array String Matching Intuition \n In the \"Intuition\" section, you would describe your initial thoughts and ideas on how to approach and solve the problem. This is where you share your initial understanding of the problem, any insights you've gained, and any high-level strategies that come to mind. It's a place to express your initial reactions and thoughts before diving into the details of your solution. \n Approach \n \n The function isAcronym takes two inputs: an array of words (words) and a string (s). \n It first checks if the length of the words array is the same as the length of the string s. If they have different lengths, it means there's a mismatch in the number of characters, and the function immediately returns false because it's not possible to form an acronym. \n If the lengths are the same, the code enters a loop that iterates through each index i from 0 to the length of the words array minus 1. \n Inside the loop, the code compares the first character of the i-th word in the words array with the i-th character in the string s. This comparison checks whether the first letter of the current word matches the corresponding character in the string. \n If any of these comparisons fail (i.e., if the characters don't match), it indicates that the acronym formation is incorrect, and the function immediately returns false. \n If all comparisons succeed (i.e., the first characters of all words match the corresponding characters in the string), the function concludes that the acronym is formed correctly and returns true after the loop completes. \n \n Complexity \n \n \n Time complexity:  O(n) \n The loop runs for words.length iterations. \nEach iteration involves a constant-time operation: comparing the first character of words[i] with s[i]. \nTherefore, the time complexity is O(n), where n is the length of the input arrays words and s. \n \n \n Space complexity:  O(1) \nThe main memory usage comes from the input arrays words and s. \nThere are also a few variables used in the loop (e.g., i). \nSince the memory usage doesn't increase with the input size, the space complexity is O(1), indicating constant space usage. \n \n \n Code \n  \n \n var   isAcronym   =   function   ( words ,  s )   { \n    if   ( words . length   !==  s . length   )   return   false ; \n \n    for   ( let  i  =   0 ;  i  <  words . length ;  i ++ )   { \n      if   ( words [ i ] [ 0 ]   !==  s [ i ] )   return   false ; \n    } \n   \n    return   true ; \n } ; Comments (0) No comments yet. 1 2 3 4 5 6 class   Solution  { public:      bool   isAcronym ( vector < string > &   words ,  string   s ) {              } }; Saved Ln 1, Col 1 You need to  Login / Sign up  to run or submit words = [\"alice\",\"bob\",\"charlie\"] s = \"abc\" 1 [\"alice\",\"bob\",\"charlie\"] Source word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1",
      "All Solutions Simple Solution adhilalikappil 64 61 Apr 03, 2024 JavaScript Intuition \n\n Approach \n\n Complexity \n \n Time complexity: \n \n\n \n Space complexity: \n \n\n Code \n  \n var   isAcronym   =   function ( words ,  s )   { \n \n    let  res  =   '' \n      for ( let  v  of  words ) { \n         res  +=  v [ 0 ] \n      } \n      return  res  ===  s\n     \n } ; Comments (0) No comments yet. 1 2 3 4 5 6 class   Solution  { public:      bool   isAcronym ( vector < string > &   words ,  string   s ) {              } }; Saved Ln 1, Col 1 You need to  Login / Sign up  to run or submit words = [\"alice\",\"bob\",\"charlie\"] s = \"abc\" 1 [\"alice\",\"bob\",\"charlie\"] Source word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1"
