      "Using Arithmatic series formulae Kabilan_C 2 16 May 14, 2024 JavaScript Code \n  \n var   maximizeSum   =   function   ( nums ,  k )   { \n      // The formula for the sum of an arithmetic series is: \n      // sum= (n/2)*(2*a + (n-1)*d) \n      // n is the number of terms in the series \n      // a is the first term of the series \n      // d is the common difference between consecutive terms. \n      let  a =   Math . max ( ... nums ) \n      return   ( k / 2 ) * ( 2 * a  +   ( k - 1 ) ) \n } ; \n \n \n Comments (0) No comments yet.",
      "All Solutions ✅ Javascript Simple Code 76 Ms beats 100% O(n) time O(1) space deleted_user 4758 167 Jul 27, 2023 JavaScript Approach \n\n <img src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/users/images/f54548fc-c439-428e-a5f9-dedb14591a37_1690517472.5807898.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2023-07-28 at 12.11.02.png\"> \n Code \n  \n var   maximizeSum   =   function   ( nums ,  k )   { \n    // Using Math.max for find max number \n    let  max  =   Math . max ( ... nums ) ; \n    // init sum \n    let  sum  =   0 ; \n    // we only need max number plus one until k \n    for   ( let  i  =   0 ;  i  <  k ;  i ++ )   { \n     sum  +=  max ; \n     max  +=   1 ; \n    } \n    // yeah that's it finally return the sum \n    return  sum ; \n } ; \n \n Complexity \n \n Time complexity: O(n) \n \n\n \n Space complexity: O(1) \n \n Comments (0) No comments yet. 1 2 3 4 5 6 class   Solution  { public:      int   maximizeSum ( vector < int > &   nums ,  int   k ) {              } }; Saved Ln 1, Col 1 You need to  Login / Sign up  to run or submit nums = [1,2,3,4,5] k = 3 1 [1,2,3,4,5] Source word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1",
      "Javascript Easiest solution. Muhsin-42 11 278 May 30, 2023 JavaScript Intuition \n The code appears to aim at finding the maximum sum by selecting the maximum element from the given array nums and adding k consecutive integers starting from 0. \n Approach \n \n Find the maximum element in the array using Math.max(...nums). \n Initialize the variable sum with the maximum element. \n Iterate k-1 times starting from 1 (since we have already accounted for 0 in the maximum element). \n In each iteration, add the current maximum element plus the current iteration index to the sum. \n Return the final sum. \n \n Complexity \n \n Time complexity: O(k) \n \n\n \n Space complexity: O(1) \n \n\n Code \n  \n var   maximizeSum   =   function ( nums ,  k )   { \n      let  max  =   Math . max ( ... nums ) ; \n     sum  =  max ; \n      for ( let  i = 1 ;  i < k ;  i ++ ) { \n         sum +=  max + i ; \n      } \n      return  sum ; \n } ; Comments (1) whales70 Jun 20, 2023 Math.max(...nums) takes O(n) time to run so the solution would be O(n+k) time 0 Show 1 Replies Reply",
      "All Solutions Beginner friendly solution in js __Gopi__ 6 2 12 hours ago JavaScript Intuition \n\n Approach \n\n Complexity \n \n Time complexity: \n \n\n \n Space complexity: \n \n\n Code \n  \n var   maximizeSum   =   function ( nums ,  k )   { \n \n \n      let  sum = 0 \n \n      let  sorted = nums . sort ( ( a , b ) => b - a ) \n \n      for ( let  i = 0 ; i < k ; i ++ ) { \n \n         sum = sum + sorted [ 0 ] + i\n      } \n \n      return  sum\n \n     \n \n \n    \n \n         \n \n \n \n \n \n \n     \n } ; Comments (0) No comments yet. 1 2 3 4 5 6 class   Solution  { public:      int   maximizeSum ( vector < int > &   nums ,  int   k ) {              } }; Saved Ln 1, Col 1 You need to  Login / Sign up  to run or submit nums = [1,2,3,4,5] k = 3 1 [1,2,3,4,5] Source word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1",
      "All Solutions ✅Beats 98.65% with just 2 lines of code😱 | step by step explanation🔥 SumitPokhriyal 95 76 Jun 04, 2023 JavaScript TypeScript Array Greedy <img src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/users/images/a9af8941-e4e0-48a3-a1f0-39d303cb6539_1685936382.6902094.png\" alt=\"Screenshot (19).png\"> \n Intuition \n\n The problem requires finding the maximum possible sum by performing a specific operation on the given array of numbers. \n Approach \n\n \n \n let max = Math.max(...nums); - This line finds the maximum number in the nums array using the Math.max function and the spread operator (...). It spreads the array elements as individual arguments to the Math.max function, which returns the maximum value. \n \n \n return ((max + k) * (max + k - 1)/2) - (max * (max - 1) / 2 ); - This line performs the calculation to maximize the sum. It calculates the sum of consecutive numbers from 1 to the new maximum number (max + k) and subtracts the sum of consecutive numbers from 1 to the original maximum number (max). \n \n \n (max + k) * (max + k - 1)/2 calculates the sum of consecutive numbers from 1 to max + k. This is done using the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series. \n \n \n (max * (max - 1) / 2) calculates the sum of consecutive numbers from 1 to max. \n \n \n By subtracting the sum of the original range from the sum of the new range, the code obtains the difference between the two ranges, which represents the maximum possible increase in the sum. \n \n \n \n \n Complexity \n \n Time complexity: O(n) - The code has a linear time complexity as it iterates through the array to find the maximum number. \n Space complexity: O(1) - The code has a constant space complexity as it does not use additional space that grows with the input size; it only utilizes a few scalar variables. \n \n Code \n function maximizeSum ( nums :  number [ ] ,  k :  number ) :  number  { \n     let  max   =  Math . max ( . . . nums ) ; \n      return   ( ( max   +  k )   *   ( max   +  k  -   1 ) / 2 )   -   ( max   *   ( max   -   1 )   /   2   ) \n } ; Comments (0) No comments yet. 1 2 3 4 5 6 class   Solution  { public:      int   maximizeSum ( vector < int > &   nums ,  int   k ) {              } }; Saved Ln 1, Col 1 You need to  Login / Sign up  to run or submit nums = [1,2,3,4,5] k = 3 1 [1,2,3,4,5] Source word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word word mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1 mmMwWLliI0fiflO&1"
