      "✅☑[C++/Java/Python/JavaScript] || Beats 100% || EXPLAINED🔥 MarkSPhilip31 8532 587 Dec 09, 2023 C++ Java Python3 C 1+ PLEASE UPVOTE IF IT HELPED \n \n Approaches \n (Also explained in the code) \n \n It iterates through the vector, starting from index 0, and checks if the battery percentage is greater than 0. \n If it's greater than 0, it increments the cnt (tested devices count) and decreases the battery percentages of subsequent devices by 1 (ensuring they don't go below 0). \n \n Complexity \n \n \n Time complexity: \n O(n)O(n) O ( n ) \n \n \n Space complexity: \n O(1)O(1) O ( 1 ) \n \n \n Code \n C++ C Java Python3 JavaScript // Function to count the number of tested devices \n function   countTestedDevices ( bp )   { \n      const  n  =  bp . length ;   // Size of the battery percentage array \n      let  cnt  =   0 ;   // Counter for tested devices \n \n      for   ( let  i  =   0 ;  i  <  n ;   ++ i )   { \n          if   ( bp [ i ]   >   0 )   { \n              ++ cnt ;   // Increment tested devices count \n              for   ( let  j  =  i  +   1 ;  j  <  n ;   ++ j )   { \n                  // Decrement battery percentage by 1, ensuring it doesn't go below 0 \n                 bp [ j ]   =   Math . max ( 0 ,  bp [ j ]   -   1 ) ; \n              } \n          } \n      } \n \n      return  cnt ;   // Return the count of tested devices \n } \n \n \n \n PLEASE UPVOTE IF IT HELPED \n \n \n Comments (6) omkarxpatel Dec 17, 2023 this is O(n^2) 3 Reply gneginskiy Dec 09, 2023 2 Show 1 Replies Reply chrischika Dec 11, 2023 Read more 1 Reply KondalDurgam Dec 09, 2023 Upvoted I did same!! bro 1 Reply ayushnemmaniwar12 Dec 09, 2023 Nice Solution, \nHello everyone! 🌟 I've got an awesome video explanation for the problem. Trust me, it's packed with logic building and proofs, and I promise you'll grasp the approach effortlessly. 🚀✨. \n https://leetcode.com/problems/count-tested-devices-after-test-operations/solutions/4385249/easy-video-solution-brute-optimal/ 1 Reply yinboshi13 Dec 10, 2023 This has quadratic time complexity for [1,2,3,4...] 0 Show 1 Replies Reply",
