      "✅ Beats 94.41 %🔥 || within 4 Lines of Code || Hash Table 🚀 || Gourav-2002 3590 3250 Oct 29, 2023 C++ Java Python3 C# 6+ <img src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/users/images/0b405fc3-359f-4627-9bba-68d8cab06268_1698634368.229628.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2023-10-30 at 8.19.03 AM.png\"> \n Intuition: \n Here we use a dictionary to store the number of 1's in the binary representation of each number in the array. Then we sort the keys of the dictionary and for each key we sort the values in the dictionary. Finally we return the sorted values. \n Algorithm: Hash Table \n \n Create a dictionary \"D\" with keys as the number of 1's in the binary representation of each number in the array and values as the numbers in the array. \n Sort the keys of the dictionary. \n For each key in the sorted keys of the dictionary, sort the values of the dictionary. \n Return the sorted values of the dictionary. \n \n Complexity Analysis: \n \n Time Complexity:  O(NlogN)  where N is the length of the array. \n Space Complexity:  O(N)  where N is the length of the array. \n \n Please UpVote⬆️ if this helps you:) \n Code \n Python C++ Java C# JavaScript TypeScript PHP  \n var   sortByBits   =   function ( arr )   { \n      const   D   =   new   Map ( ) ; \n \n          for   ( let  i  of  arr )   { \n              const  count  =  i . toString ( 2 ) . split ( '1' ) . length   -   1 ; \n              if   ( ! D . has ( count ) )   { \n                  D . set ( count ,   [ ] ) ; \n              } \n              D . get ( count ) . push ( i ) ; \n          } \n \n          const  result  =   [ ] ; \n          for   ( let  k  of   [ ... D . keys ( ) ] . sort ( ( a ,  b )   =>  a  -  b ) )   { \n              D . get ( k ) . sort ( ( a ,  b )   =>  a  -  b ) ; \n             result . push ( ... D . get ( k ) ) ; \n          } \n \n          return  result ; \n } ; \n <img src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/users/images/d08b3acb-9eec-44d6-b377-0de7969557e5_1698635425.249877.png\" alt=\"image.png\"> Comments (5) Gourav-2002 Oct 29, 2023 👇 Please UpVote ⬆️ here if you found this helpful. 7 Reply owenwu4 Nov 29, 2023 please stop writing code that is hard to read - return [i for k in sorted(D.keys()) for i in sorted(D[k])] - you're wasting time 1 Reply whovianzoro Oct 30, 2023 used the same logic, but i made it way less elegant! cool! 0 Show 1 Replies Reply sourav_n06 Oct 29, 2023 ✅ Beats 99.41 %🔥 || Bit Manipulation || Google C++ 🚀 || \n https://leetcode.com/problems/sort-integers-by-the-number-of-1-bits/solutions/4224986/beats-99-41-bit-manipulation-google-c/ \n Click To Check Right Now --> 0 Reply SergeyZhirkov Oct 29, 2023 Please Upvote my solution, if you find it helpful :) \nEasy 1 line solution (Java Stream) \n https://leetcode.com/problems/sort-integers-by-the-number-of-1-bits/solutions/4224416/easy-1-line-solution-java-stream/ 0 Reply"
