      "JS - Faster than 97% - Using Sets nilsonmolina 30 1351 May 31, 2019 JavaScript var   repeatedNTimes   =   function ( A )   { \n    let  lookup  =   new   Set ( ) ; \n \n    for   ( let  n  of   A )   { \n      if   ( lookup . has ( n ) )   return  n ; \n     lookup . add ( n ) ; \n    } \n \n    return   - 1 ; \n } ; Comments (5) habdou Dec 17, 2019 OK, the  Set  is much faster:  http://jsben.ch/ASDpk 2 Reply vaibhavgattyani32 Apr 25, 2022 You don't need the last return statement because it is mentioned in the question that there is exactly 1 value that is repeating. 1 Reply habdou Dec 17, 2019 Read more 1 Show 1 Replies Reply umangvyas94 Sep 18, 2023 One liner - \n return nums.find(num => nums.indexOf(num) != nums.lastIndexOf(num) ) 0 Reply Omhet Aug 26, 2019 Nice one! 0 Reply",
      "All Solutions Javascript O(n) zeroabsolute 10 351 Aug 22, 2020 JavaScript var   repeatedNTimes   =   function ( A )   { \n      const  map  =   { } ; \n     \n      for   ( let  i  =   0 ;  i  <   A . length ;  i ++ )   { \n          if   ( A [ i ]   in  map )   { \n              return   A [ i ] ; \n          }   else   { \n             map [ A [ i ] ]   =   0 ; \n          } \n      } \n     \n      return   0 ; \n } ; Comments (0) No comments yet. 1 2 3 4 5 6 class   Solution  { public:      int   repeatedNTimes ( vector < int > &   nums ) {              } };",
      "Solution beats 99% in runtime and 93% in memory. Optimized way muhammedsheheem 5 180 Aug 24, 2023 JavaScript Intuition \n\n The unique number is half + 1 of the length of array. \nAnd one number is half of the length of array. \nWhich means the half of the array is unique and the rest is same number. So we just have to find the duplicate from the array. \n Eg :- \nnums = [2,1,2,5,3,2] \n nums.length = 6 \nn = 3 ( nums.length == 2 * n ) \n Here uniques are 1, 2, 3, 5 => length = 4 \n unique   =   [   1 ,   2 ,   3 ,   5   ]  length  =   4 \n restOfArray  =   [   2 ,   2   ]  length  =   2 \n \n As per question a single element repeats 3 times \n restOfArray = [ 2, 2 ] \n Here 2 repeats two times and unique array have the another 2 \nwhich means 2 is coming three times \n This may feels Complicated \n The conclusion is : \n1 numer repeats n times \nLook at the array mentioned above \nHalf of the array do not repeat and the other half will be the same number \n So we just have to find the repeating element \n Note that there will be only one element that repeats!!! \n Approach \n\n First I did normal nested loop to find the duplicate. if one number matches the other, i returned the number. because there will be only one number that repeats. \n Then I optimised it with Set() \n Complexity \n \n Time complexity: O(n) \n \n\n \n Space complexity: O(n) \n \n\n Code \n  \n var   repeatedNTimes   =   function ( nums )   { \n      const  arrSet  =   new   Set ( ) ; \n      for   ( const  item  of  nums )   { \n          if   ( arrSet . has ( item ) )   { \n              return  item ; \n          } \n         arrSet . add ( item ) ; \n      } \n } ; Comments (1) vinhphamdev0406 Aug 27, 2023 if test case is  nums = [1, 2, 3, 3, 4, 2, 4, 4], can it pass? 1 Show 1 Replies Reply",
